-- title:
--   Serre–Tate lifting step: from 𝔪ⁿ to 𝔪ⁿ⁺¹
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \neq 2$ (a prime instance for $q$ being assumed), a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and an elliptic Weierstrass curve $E_0$ over $k$ whose formal group satisfies `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, that is, taking the ideal $\bot$ as the defining ideal, there is a unit power series $u$ with `nthSeries q` of $E_0.\mathrm{formalGroup}$ equal to $u$ times its `drinfeldDivisor q 0 0`. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal, with maximal ideal generated by $q$, and $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ a surjective ring map with kernel that maximal ideal. Let $T$ be an Artinian local commutative $W_0$-algebra with a surjective ring map $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ whose kernel is $\mathfrak m_T$ and which agrees with $\mathrm{res}_0$ on the image of $W_0$. Let $G$ be a commutative formal group over $T$ with $E_0.\mathrm{formalGroup}$ obtained from $G$ by applying $\mathrm{res}_T$ coefficientwise. Let $n \geq 1$. Assume there exist a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $T$ with $E.\mathrm{map}\ \mathrm{res}_T = E_0$, a formal group $G_n$ over $T/\mathfrak m_T^n$ whose law is the law `formalGroupLawFixed` of the reduction of $E$ modulo $\mathfrak m_T^n$, and an isomorphism of formal group laws $\psi$ from $G_n$ to the reduction of $G$ modulo $\mathfrak m_T^n$ (a power series with zero constant term, unit linear coefficient, commuting with the two laws) all of whose coefficients are congruent to those of $X$ modulo the image of $\mathfrak m_T$ in $T/\mathfrak m_T^n$. Then the same data exist with $n$ replaced by $n+1$.
--
--   This is the inductive step of the Serre–Tate existence argument: a Weierstrass lift of $E_0$ whose formal group law is identified with that of $G$ modulo $\mathfrak m_T^n$, by an isomorphism congruent to the identity, can be replaced by one with the identification valid modulo $\mathfrak m_T^{n+1}$, the step across the small extension $\mathfrak m_T^n/\mathfrak m_T^{n+1}$. It feeds the induction on the nilpotency index of $\mathfrak m_T$ carried out in [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_map_eq_and_lawIso_of_isBaseChange_formalGroup_of_isArtinianRing`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_map_eq_and_lawIso_of_isBaseChange_formalGroup_of_isArtinianRing).
